  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $(A_i)$ be a family of countably infinite sets such that $\\lvert A_i\\cap A_j\\rvert \neq 2$ for all $i\neq j$. Find the smallest cardinal $C$ such that $\\cup A_i$ can always be coloured with at most $C$ colours so that no $A_i$ is monochromatic.",
